# Line-ending policy: this is a Windows-first project, so text files use CRLF in the working
# tree. Git stores LF-normalized blobs and converts to CRLF on checkout; `text=auto` also lets
# git auto-detect and leave binary files alone. Committing this makes the policy repo-wide, so
# it no longer depends on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never apply line-ending conversion.
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.lockb  binary
